        n.facing = ...; n.x = nx; n.y = ny; n.px = nx; n.py = ny;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Immediate teleport move is jarring but subtle once per ~1.5s per NPC; acceptable "activity". Better: set n.from/to and moving with progress — needs per-npc movement state. Simpler teleport is fine for prototype ("NPC activity"). Actually let me do proper smooth: add `n.pending`... too much. Teleport with a 6-frame snap: set px,py to current, then target; interpolation next frames... world.js only interpolates player. Keep teleport; it's slight but readable as "wandering". Hmm, teleporting NPCs look glitchy. Alternative: only change facing occasionally + rare step teleport. I'll do: 70% just change facing (idle activity), 30% step if walkable. Still teleport for step. Fine.

Let me add wanderAcc to world object init and logic.

OK, write zones.js hearthfall replacement now.

