Wait — there's a bug: in world-mode choice, `d.resolveChoice` is set, and `ui.resolveChoice` is NOT set (DOM one). So `ui.dialogueOpen && ui.resolveChoice` is false in world mode — the canvas branch handles it. But in DOM mode, `ui.dialogueOpen` set true, `ui.resolveChoice` set. Good.

But `advanceDialogue()` in world mode: I redefined it to handle d. Good.

Also `finishTyping` defined but unused — remove later if lint complains; harmless.

Now `updateHud` — still updates DOM; fine.

Also `showInteract` now sets ui.nearLabel — but I changed its signature behavior: it still shows DOM prompt. The DOM `.interact-prompt` remains; I'll hide it via CSS in world mode? The DOM prompt shows at bottom center; canvas one draws above object. Having both is redundant. CSS: `.interact-prompt { display: none; }` — but it's used nowhere else. Fine, hide it.

